nodecode-muse is a rewrite of xiaohei-info's xiaohei-info/hermes-muse:

  https://github.com/xiaohei-info/hermes-muse
  commit 0dade28130b6901dfa2dd81a067856441948d33c
  MIT License, Copyright (c) 2026 xiaohei-info (LICENSE)

The original is a Hermes assembly: one `muse_manage` tool over forty actions,
six Cron jobs (`memory-upkeep`, `nightly-review`, `feed-pulse` and their
reviews), a Skill with fourteen references, a Dashboard and a Desktop page,
holding goals, expiring interests, ideas, Feed articles, reminder candidates,
research runs and operation findings in one SQLite-and-files store, with
revisions and request ids on every write. What this rewrite keeps is the part
a person asks for by name: the same tool name and the original's action names
for goals, interests, ideas, the Feed, reminders, the Feed brief and
forgetting, the arguments still inside one `data` object, and the fields the
original's Skill documents for each (title, description, completion criteria,
deadline, status active/done/cancelled, a note on completion, expiring
interests, Feed sources and why, due reminders resolved as done, dismissed,
stopped or snoozed). Objects carry the integer revision the original's
`expected_revision` compares, and a Feed article's key still makes one
article out of one event. The one page a user reads -- goals, the Feed and
reminders -- is `/muse` and the panel it opens, and (help :muse) is the
procedure text the Skill carried. State is one JSON file under the home
instead of SQLite plus a content tree, so a person can read it.

Left out, and why: the six Cron jobs (this rewrite runs nothing while a
session idles -- a due reminder is handed to the next model request instead),
background research and delegation to subagents, the memory-upkeep and
self-review procedures with their operation audit and findings, calendar and
source-check windows, content paging with cursors, the read-only Dashboard
/FastAPI router and the Desktop page, and the multi-profile management. They
are each a large surface of their own, and all of them rest on Hermes Cron,
Hermes delegation and Hermes' Dashboard that a Nodecode cell does not have.
Nothing of the original is vendored: no Python, no Node, no Hermes imports.
